    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="section faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="faq-layout">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">05 · Questions</p>
          <h2 id="faq-title">The right questions before you make the switch.</h2>
          <p>From connecting ClinTa Extended to running your whole laboratory workflow.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-grid" data-faq>
          <details open>
            <summary><span>01</span> What makes ClinTa LARIS a Lab ERP rather than just laboratory software?</summary>
            <p>
              Laboratory software stops at tests and reports. LARIS also runs billing, stock, HR,
              accounts and the patient portal on one shared patient record.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><span>02</span> Is ClinTa LARIS suitable for my laboratory, regardless of its size?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes. Single-department labs start with the core modules, multi-department labs run all
              ten, and modules can be switched on as you grow.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><span>03</span> What reporting and insights can I get from ClinTa LARIS?</summary>
            <p>
              Each role gets its own dashboard, and Admin sees turnaround times, workload,
              productivity, compliance and profit and loss in one place.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><span>04</span> Is ClinTa LARIS easy to learn and use?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes. Each person learns only the screens for their role, handoffs between modules are
              automatic, and we train each team during rollout.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><span>05</span> How secure is ClinTa LARIS for patient records?</summary>
            <p>
              Access is role-based, patients sign in securely to see their own reports, and every
              report change is kept in an amendment history.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

